# VideoBrief — Architecture

## Layout

```text
Browser
  → Next.js (RSC + thin Server Actions + TanStack Query where needed)
      → domain/application logic (analysis pipeline lives here)
          → Drizzle / Supabase
          → TranscriptProvider (youtubei.js)
          → AIProvider (Vercel AI SDK + Claude Haiku)
```

Server Actions authenticate, authorize, validate input, then call domain functions. **Do not** embed the analysis pipeline in actions or React components.

Structure domain code so it can later move behind a queue without rewrite. Do **not** add Redis/workers until a concrete timeout/requirement appears.

## Per-user video data

Each library entry is one row per `(user_id, youtube_id)`:

- `user_videos` — metadata + English transcript snapshot (refreshed on every ingest/re-paste)
- `personalized_analyses` — analysis state machine (1:1 with `user_videos`)

Re-pasting the same URL **always refetches** from YouTube and upserts that user's row. There is **no shared global cache** of videos/transcripts across users.

Also per-user:

- `user_context` / topic context / preferences
- `video_context` (video-specific answers, later)
- personalized sections / takeaways (later columns or tables)

Classification (`isEducational`, domains, section skeleton) lands on the user video or analysis row in a later slice — not a shared `videos` table.

## Analysis states

Keep the state machine simple, e.g.:

`pending` → `fetching_transcript` → `analyzing` → `awaiting_context` → `generating_summary` → `complete` | `failed`

- Skip `awaiting_context` when not educational (or when no useful questions remain).
- UI should communicate progress without leaking internals.

## Suggested folder sketch

```text
src/
  app/                 # routes, layouts, loading/error
  components/          # UI (shadcn + feature)
  domain/              # analysis pipeline, pure-ish business logic
  db/                  # drizzle schema, client
  lib/                 # supabase, ai, youtube, utils, actions
  hooks/
  messages/            # next-intl (en.json)
```

## Cost awareness

Reuse intermediate structured analysis per user where possible; avoid re-sending full transcripts on LLM retries; skip known context questions; Haiku for all MVP LLM calls.
